 "equipment_type": "Rooftop unit controller (TEC zoning system)",
 "applies_to": "Constant volume, pressure-dependent rooftop units with up to two heating and two cooling stages and a bypass damper, run by the TEC2664Z-3 rooftop controller of the Johnson Controls TEC zoning system.",
 "summary": "The TEC2664Z-3 is the rooftop controller of the Johnson Controls TEC zoning system. It collects heating and cooling demand from its TEC2647Z-3 zone controllers over BACnet MS/TP, stages the rooftop fan, cooling and heating outputs, controls the bypass damper on duct static pressure, and holds the system occupancy schedule. It exposes the discharge, return and outdoor temperatures, stage status, zone demand data and alarms.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": "76aaa (aaa = MS/TP address)",
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Objects from Table 24 of the TEC zoning technical bulletin (LIT-12011682), pages 64-67; the device object (TEC2664Z-76aaa) is not listed as a point.",
  "Access follows the table footnotes. The schedule object (SCH 1) is readable only; the bulletin says it is not writable from any controller.",
  "The -2 edition of the bulletin (TEC2664Z-2) lists the same objects except Cfg Deadband (AV 22).",
  "Temperatures are listed in °F; the bulletin also gives the °C range."
 ],
 "source": {
